1887 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (THE HEART IS THE CENTRAL ORGAN OF THE CARDIOVASCULAR SYSTEM.  IT IS A MUSCULAR PUMP WHICH CONTRACTS & RELAXES RHYTHMICALLY TO CIRCULATE BLOOD THROUGHOUT THE BODY.  THE HEART HAS FOUR CHAMBERS: TWO ATRIA \(UPPER CHAMBERS\) & TWO VENTRICLES \(LOWER CHAMBERS\).  IT RECEIVES BLOOD FROM THE BODY & PUMPS IT TO THE LUNGS FOR OXYGENATION & THEN RECEIVES OXYGENATED BLOOD FROM THE LUNGS & PUMPS IT OUT TO THE REST OF THE BODY.)
/E (THE HEART IS THE CENTRAL ORGAN OF THE CARDIOVASCULAR SYSTEM.  IT IS A MUSCULAR PUMP WHICH CONTRACTS & RELAXES RHYTHMICALLY TO CIRCULATE BLOOD THROUGHOUT THE BODY.  THE HEART HAS FOUR CHAMBERS: TWO ATRIA \(UPPER CHAMBERS\) & TWO VENTRICLES \(LOWER CHAMBERS\).  IT RECEIVES BLOOD FROM THE BODY & PUMPS IT TO THE LUNGS FOR OXYGENATION & THEN RECEIVES OXYGENATED BLOOD FROM THE LUNGS & PUMPS IT OUT TO THE REST OF THE BODY.)
/Pg 90 0 R
/K [0]
>>
